  "solution": {
    "approach": "Read the integer T. Then loop T times, reading a whole line (including spaces) for each test case. Immediately output the line unchanged. No processing is required beyond correct line reading, because the task is to echo the input strings.",
    "timeComplexity": "O(T * L) where L is the average length of a line (at most 100).",
    "spaceComplexity": "O(L) for the buffer that holds one line at a time.",
    "code": {
      "C": "#include <stdio.h>\n#include <string.h>\nint main() {\n    int T;\n    if (scanf(\"%d\", &T) != 1) return 0;\n    getchar(); // consume the newline after T\n    char line[101];\n    while (T--) {\n        if (fgets(line, sizeof(line), stdin) == NULL) {\n            line[0] = '\\0';\n        }\n        line[strcspn(line, \"\\n\")] = '\\0'; // remove trailing newline\n        printf(\"%s\\n\", line);\n    }\n    return 0;\n}",
      "C++": "#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n    int T;\n    if (!(cin >> T)) return 0;\n    string line;\n    getline(cin, line); // consume end‑of‑line after T\n    while (T--) {\n        getline(cin, line);\n        cout << line << '\\n';\n    }\n    return 0;\n}",
      "Java": "import java.io.*;\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        int T = Integer.parseInt(br.readLine().trim());\n        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();\n        for (int i = 0; i < T; i++) {\n            String line = br.readLine();\n            if (line == null) line = \"\";\n            sb.append(line);\n            if (i < T - 1) sb.append('\\n');\n        }\n        System.out.print(sb.toString());\n    }\n}",
      "Python3": "import sys\ndata = sys.stdin.read().splitlines()\nif not data:\n    sys.exit()\nT = int(data[0])\nlines = data[1:1+T]\nprint('\\n'.join(lines))",
      "JavaScript": "const fs = require('fs');\nconst input = fs.readFileSync(0, 'utf-8').split('\\n');\nconst T = parseInt(input[0], 10);\nlet out = [];\nfor (let i = 1; i <= T; i++) {\n  out.push(input[i] ?? '');\n}\nprocess.stdout.write(out.join('\\n'));\n"
    },
